#
# === What @trust IS (five load-bearing properties) ===
#
# 1. Content-addressed — every chain-step is a content-addressed
#    OID; tampering with any step breaks every subsequent OID.
# 2. Non-forgeable — only the root-holder can authorize the next
#    evolution step (SSH-key holder / passkey-holder).
# 3. Root-terminating — every chain terminates at a @subject root
#    (typically @alex for mirror-substrate; any human_a per SEL §1).
# 4. Two-altitude admissible — the same substrate-decl'd chain
#    admits BOTH SSH-signing at compiler AND passkey/PRF at garden.
# 5. Additive / append-only — chains only grow; multiple-key
#    superseding per bridge §"The Mapping".
#
# === Two altitudes of the SAME chain ===
#
# Per canonical spec §2 (full table there). Summary:
#
#   Compiler altitude (SSH):
#     root artifact  — ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#     auth proof     — ed25519 signature over commit tree
#     chain step     — git commit (SSH-signed)
#     content hash   — git SHA-1 (interop) / SHA-256 (canonical)
#
#   Garden altitude (Passkey/PRF):
#     root artifact  — WebAuthn credential in secure enclave
#     auth proof     — HMAC-SHA-256 PRF over server salt
#     chain step     — spectral_state evolution (SHA-512 fold)
#     content hash   — SHA-512(prev || prf_output || entropy)
#
# Both compose over @io/crypto at mechanism boundary. Both terminate
# at same @subject root (typically @alex). Both discharge chain_
# terminates_at_root(step, root) per canonical spec §5.
#
# === The 5-op prism inherits @void basis ===
#
# Per Recognition #79 (5-op basis IS Void's tongue) + shards/void.
# mirror §Composition inheritance discipline: every family-root
# inherits Void's basis. @trust names the inheritance below without
# `in @void` explicit import per closure discipline.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain (audit clean) ===
#
# Grep verdict clean at family-root altitude for `@trust`:
#
# - `@trust` as family-root: does NOT exist prior to this landing.
# - `trust_root`: appears only in narrative sentences grounding
#   landings (e.g. shards/tool/git.mirror:23 "The @trust chain
#   terminates at @alex"; shards/tool.mirror:229 comment).
# - `trust_chain` / `signed_at_alex_root`: appear as named predicate
#   in shards/epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_
#   witnessed.mirror as the DEFERRED-RED conjunct 4 whose discharge
#   awaits this family-root landing.
#
# The word `trust` was substrate-decl'd across ~14 months of SSH-
# signing bootstrap history + closure spec §6.2 + StageFreight spec
# conjunct 4 forward-promise + passkey-spectral-bridge insight + Alex
# 2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent. This landing NAMES what was
# implicit at family-root altitude. ~62nd instance of [[feedback-
# substrate-already-had-the-word]].
